    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a2">

                <pb facs="0483" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg473"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 4 in No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Tupper to Mr.
                        Gunnison.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax, Nova
                            Scotia,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 14, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have it in command from his honor the
                    administrator of the government to inform you, in reply to your communication
                    respecting the Chesapeake, that the question has been referred to the crown
                    officers, and that they are of opinion that they do not see upon what grounds,
                    as at present informed, they can legally interfere.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. TUPPER, <hi rendition="#italic">Provincial
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
